  "reason": "The best result so far is config_014 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted; acc=0.713). The evidence strongly supports transformer aggregation (+0.035 over avgpool) and scvi_n200 (+0.039 over pca_n2000). The key remaining uncertainty in this top-performing regime is the image encoder: with pca_n2000+avgpool, resnet50 and imagenet_vit_l were nearly tied, but under transformer aggregation the larger ViT-L's richer representations may interact differently. Config_024 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) is a single-variable change from config_014, directly testing whether imagenet_vit_l can push accuracy beyond 0.713. This is the highest-value exploitation step: it extends the strongest configuration along the one untested axis, and with 5 experiments remaining, confirming or ruling out the image encoder choice early allows the remaining budget to focus on further refinements (e.g., fusion strategy or scgpt) if needed."
}

